# Auto-upload — Cursor Rules

## Output Style (Caveman Mode)

- Ultra-concise. Code/diff-first. Zero filler, greetings, or throat-clearing.
- Prefer patches and file paths over prose. Explain only when architecture or risk is unclear.
- No restating the task. No “here’s what I did” essays.

## Repository Map (do not invent paths)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `run_sync.py` | Primary CLI entry (scrape / plan / execute sync) |
| `config.yaml` | Accounts, sync caps, FB location, renew/repost |
| `.env` / `.env.example` | Secrets & runtime toggles (`DRY_RUN`, delays, paths) |
| `src/inventory/` | autosell.mx scrape + catalog snapshots |
| `src/sync/` | Diff engine, repost planning |
| `src/store/` | `sync.db` persistence |
| `src/facebook/` | Playwright Marketplace workers |
| `src/quote_engine/` | Phase 2 — local French Amortization calculator |
| `src/odoo_sync/` | Phase 2 — Odoo XML-RPC (CRM + WhatsApp + Fleet + Documents) |
| `src/whatsapp_worker/` | Phase 2 — open-wa / Evolution API wrapper |
| `src/voice_gateway/` | Phase 2 — FastAPI voice + Meta webhook entry |
| `src/meta_gateway/` | Phase 2 — Facebook Page Messenger Graph API |
| `src/pdf_engine/` | Phase 2 — ReportLab quote / vehicle spec PDF |
| `src/pipeline.py` | Phase 2 — lead orchestration (quote → Odoo → PDF → WA) |
| `src/sync/weekly_bump.py` | Alternate Sunday renew vs full repost |
| `scripts/run_weekly_bump.py` | CLI / CI entry for weekly bump |
| `scripts/` | Manual FB probes, login, debug |
| `sessions/` | Playwright browser profiles (per account) |
| `data/` | DB, snapshots, debug PNGs |
| `docs/` | System design & project guide |

**Do not restructure** existing trees under `src/`, `scripts/`, `data/`, or `sessions/`.

## Context Integration

- Entry point: `run_sync.py`. Wire new CLI flags / flows through it or dedicated `scripts/` — not ad-hoc top-level runners unless asked.
- Settings: read `config.yaml` + env via `python-dotenv`. Prefer existing helpers (`env_bool`, `env_int`, account scoping).
- Sessions: Playwright state lives in `sessions/account_*` as configured in `config.yaml`. Never commit session cookies. Never invent alternate session roots.
- Persistence: `DB_PATH` / `SNAPSHOT_DIR` from env; default `data/sync.db`, `data/snapshots`.

## Skill Hierarchy & Boundaries

### MEMORY (`claude-mem`)
- Background only: index/read project rules and design in `docs/` (esp. `docs/PROJECT_GUIDE.md`).
- Do not dump memory tooling into user-facing chat noise.

### DEVELOPMENT (`superpowers` / `ponytail`)
- IDE-side: format, refactor, static analysis.
- Match existing Python style (`from __future__ import annotations`, typed where present).

### AUTOMATION & SCRAPING
- Browser profile isolation: one profile per account under `sessions/`.
- **Never** run live browser / Playwright scripts inside the LLM chat window.
- Live FB work: operator or CI on `fb-worker` via `scripts/` / `run_sync.py`. Agent may edit code; operator runs headed login / posts.
- Scraping workers (`src/facebook/`, inventory scrape) stay isolated from messaging workers (`src/whatsapp_worker/`, `src/meta_gateway/`). No shared browser profiles, no cross-worker session reuse.

## Security & Performance

- **Secrets:** never hardcode tokens, passwords, Odoo creds, WhatsApp / Meta Page API keys. Use `.env`; document new keys in `.env.example` only as placeholders.
- **Finance:** French Amortization and all quote math run **locally in Python** inside `src/quote_engine/` (ms-scale). Compute fully before any payload to Odoo, WhatsApp, Messenger, Telegram, or other external channels. No remote calc round-trips for amortization.
- Do not log secrets, session cookies, or full `.env` contents.

## Phase 2 Module Contracts (scaffold)

- `quote_engine` — pure local finance; no network I/O.
- `odoo_sync` — CRM lead/opportunity + inventory XML-RPC; credentials from env.
- `whatsapp_worker` — outbound messaging API only; separate process/config from FB Playwright.
- `voice_gateway` — FastAPI entry for Voice AI + Meta webhook routes.
- `meta_gateway` — Page Messenger verify/parse/quote/Odoo/Graph reply; uses `FB_VERIFY_TOKEN` / `FB_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN`.

Lead path (target): Web/Voice AI / Messenger → quote (`quote_engine`) → Odoo (`odoo_sync`) → WhatsApp or Graph reply. FB Marketplace sync remains a separate pipeline via `run_sync.py`.

## Change Discipline

- Touch only files needed for the request.
- Do not commit unless explicitly asked.
- Prefer extending existing modules over parallel duplicate helpers.
